---The configuration for agent access on a stack. Agent access enables AI agents to interact with desktop applications during streaming sessions.
---@class aws.appstream.AgentAccessConfig
---@field Settings aws.appstream.AgentAccessSettingList The list of agent access settings that define permissions for each agent action. You must specify at least one setting, and at least one agent action must be enabled.
---@field S3BucketArn? aws.appstream.S3BucketArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Amazon S3 bucket where agent screenshots and Replay Session artifacts are stored. Required when ScreenshotsUploadEnabled or ReplaySessionEnabled is true.
---@field ScreenshotsUploadEnabled? aws.appstream.BooleanObject Indicates whether screenshot uploads to Amazon S3 are enabled for agent sessions.
---@field ReplaySessionEnabled? aws.appstream.BooleanObject Indicates whether Replay Session is enabled for agent sessions. WorkSpaces Applications delivers a video combining session screenshots, a transcript, and a report for each session. Requires the COMPUTER_VISION agent action.
---@field KmsKeyArn? aws.appstream.KmsKeyArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the customer managed symmetric encryption KMS key that encrypts Replay Session artifacts while WorkSpaces Applications processes them. The key must be in the same Region as the stack, and ReplaySessionEnabled must be true.
---@field ScreenResolution aws.appstream.ScreenResolution|string The screen resolution for the agent streaming environment.
---@field ScreenImageFormat aws.appstream.ScreenImageFormat|string The image format for agent screen captures.
---@field UserControlMode? aws.appstream.UserControlMode|string The user control mode for agent sessions. This setting determines how users can interact with agent sessions.

